node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# This project's lockfile is pnpm-lock.yaml — CI installs with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
# A package-lock.json here is a local artefact of someone typing `npm install` out of habit, and it
# is ignored rather than merely deleted: an 85-byte EMPTY one (`"packages": {}`) WAS tracked for two
# months beside the real lockfile, and made `npm ci` fail with an unhelpful error. Deleting it once
# would have let the next `npm install` commit it again.
package-lock.json

# The panel-shot harness's build output and its captures. `dist/` above only matches the app's own
# build; these sit under scripts/, and a PNG that is regenerated by every CI run has no business in
# git history. Evidence worth keeping is copied into progress/ deliberately, per report.
scripts/shots/dist/
scripts/shots/shots/
# …and the copies that appear when something cannot delete `dist` and renames it aside instead. Nine
# of these accumulated as UNTRACKED directories in one session, each a full copy of the bundle: they
# pollute `git status` until a reader stops looking at the list, and they are one `git add -A` away
# from being committed. Same policy as the directory they are copies of — build output never travels.
scripts/shots/dist.aside.*/
scripts/shots/dist.stale.*/
